// WoSX's default tree: FCPW's scalar binary BVH (layouts/fcpwb.bonsai), the
// walk a loop, the closest-point traversal on a stack of FCPW's depth, the
// leaf's Voronoi arms skipped where no lane needs them -- the matching
// schedule against WoSX built as it ships (FCPW_USE_ENOKI off), one thread
// against one thread. Nothing is vectorized: FCPW's scalar traversal tests
// one box and one triangle at a time, and so does this. The children are
// visited left then right where FCPW visits the nearer first (the layout
// says why).
import apps/wosx/schedules/layouts/fcpwb;

schedule {
    walk.loopify();
    closest.loopify(64);
    closest.skip(closest_point_fcpw);
}
